  FT["MY-H215"] = {"id":"MY-H215","coverage":"partial","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-detail.php?act=244&lang=BI","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":27,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"1981年马来西亚国家电影发展局法","en":"PERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM NASIONAL MALAYSIA ACT 1981","orig":"PERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM NASIONAL MALAYSIA ACT 1981","vi":"Luật về Tổng công ty Phát triển Phim Quốc gia Malaysia năm 1981","th":"พระราชบัญญัติองค์การพัฒนาภาพยนตร์แห่งชาติมาเลเซีย ค.ศ. 1981","id":"Undang-Undang Perbadanan Pengembangan Film Nasional Malaysia Tahun 1981","ms":"Akta Perbadanan Kemajuan Filem Nasional Malaysia 1981"},"level":"law","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"ACT244","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"1981","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 34 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\1981_244_PERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM NASIONAL MALAYSIA ACT 1981.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H215-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"chapter":{"en":"ParT I"},"text":{"en":"1. (1) This Act may be cited as the Perbadanan\nKemajuan Filem Nasional Malaysia Act 1981 and shall\napply throughout Malaysia.        |\n\n(2) This Act shall come into operation on such date\n.or dates as the Minister may, by notification in the\nGazette, appoint and he may appoint different dates\nfor different provisions and for different parts of\nMalaysia."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"chapter":{"en":"ParT I"},"text":{"en":"2. In this, oy cad the context otherwise requires—\n\nCiv\n\"Chairman\" means the Chairman of the Perbadanan\nappointed under section 4 and includes the Deputy\nChairman and a temporary Chairman while exercising\n\nthe functions of the Chairman;\n\n\"chief executive officer\" means the chief executive\nofficer of the Perbadanan appointed under section 9;\n\n\"cinema hall\" includes any premises, building,\nstructure and any place whatsoever used to screen films\nfor viewing by the public or any class of the public;\n\nShort title,                  |\napplication               3\nand com-\nmencement.\n\nK S198 /\nSept fart V™\nCPu(Bd2E5]81)\n\nny\nInterpreta-\ntion.         AAS\n\n(Pt. I-II, S. 2-3]\n6                              Acr 244\n\nlng BDA        Te                                  Sherk Wye} An,\nA         PM    yy.                  h   fil      .\nplus,        films\" includes feature films, short films/ftrailers,\n       As     documentaries, advertising filmlets and any Tecording\n\n|          pineludtnp on material of any kingof moving images, accompanied\n;  In, PADA  wipes    discs OT unaccompanied indo for viewing by the public\nks        or any class of the public;                  ,                 |\n\"film activities\" includes all activities related to the\n\nfilm industry;\n\n\"¥                \"film distribution\" includes the renting, hiring and\n\n|                            loaning of films for profit or otherwise, the importation\n\n              and distribution of films produced abroad and the\ndistribution of films produced locally;\n\n\"film exhibition\" means the screening of films for\nviewing by the public or any class of the public;\n\n\"film industry\" includes the activities of film pro-\nduction, distribution and exhibition carried out in\n\n(vo P        sendi\na post Su Malaysia;\ni\n\nIn.\n\n\"film production\" includes all activities related to the (\n\nAa      production or processing of films/for viewing by the\nrast       > public or any  lass, of the public;\n\n                Dinca\n               \"member\", in relation to the Perbadanan, includes\n           the Chairman, Deputy Chairman and a temporary\n             Chairman of the Perbadanan; and, in relation to a\n;                     committee of the Perbadanan, includes the chairman of\n|                the committee;\n\n\"Minister\" means the Minister charged with the\nresponsibility for the development of the film industry;\n\n\"officer of the Perbadanan\" includes the chief exe-\ncutive officer;\n\n\"Perbadanan\" means the Perbadanan Kemajuan\nFilem Nasional Malaysia established under section 3;\n\n\"prescribed\" means prescribed by subsidiary legis-\nPen    — s  lation made under this Act;\n|                              Part II\n\nPERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM\nNASIONAL MALAYSIA\n\nEstablish- 3. There shall be established a corporation by the name\nmentofthe of \"Perbadanan Kemajuan Filem Nasional Malaysia\"\nKemajuan Which shall have perpetual succession and a common\n          Filem | seal and which may sue and be sued in the same name\nMalaysia. and, subject to and for the purposes of this Act, may\n\n(Pt.   II,   S.\n\nPERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM         i\nNASIONAL MALAYSIA\n\nenter into contracts and hold and deal in or with any\nmovable or immovable property and do all other\nmatters and things incidental or appertaining to a body\ncorporate."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"chapter":{"en":"ParT I"},"text":{"en":"4. (1) The Perbadanan shall consist of a Chairman, a\nDeputy Chairman and not less than seven but not more\nthan ten other members, to be constituted as follows—\n\n(a) a Chairman and a Deputy Chairman to be\nappointed by the Minister from amongst\npersons who, in his opinion, by reason of their\nknowledge and extensive experience, would be\nof substantial service to the film industry;\n\n(5) four members to be appointed by the Minister\nfrom amongst persons who are connected with\nthe film and related industries and are not\npublic officers;                            ~—\n\n‘\n\n34]\n\nMember-\nship of the\nPerbadanan.\n\n(c) the Secretary General of the Ministry charged |\n\nwith the responsibility for the development of\nthe film industry, or his representative;\n\n(d) the Secretary General of the Ministry charged\nwith the responsibility for finance, or his repre-\nsentative;\n\n(e) the Secretary General of the Ministry charged\nwith the responsibility for information, or his\nTepresentative; and\n\n(f) such other persons, being not more than three\nin number, as the Minister considers fit and\nproper persons to be members of the Perba-\ndanan, to be appointed by the Minister.\n\n(2) A member of the Perbadanan appointed under\nparagraph (a), (b) or (f) shall, unless his appointment is\nsooner revoked or he sooner resigns, hold office for such\nperiod not exceeding three years as the Minister may\ndetermine and he shall be eligible for reappointment.\n\n(3) The members of the Perbadanan may be paid\nsuch remuneration or allowances as the Minister may\ndetermine.\n\n(4) The provisions of the Schedule shall apply in\nrespect of the Perbadanan and its members.\n\n[Pt. II, S. 5-6]\n8                  Acr 244\n\nSeni of the   5. (1) The Perbadanan shall have a common seal and\nemee™™®* such seal may, from time to time, be broken, changed,\naltered or made anew as the Perbadanan deems fit:\n\nProvided that until a seal is provided under this\nsection a stamp bearing the inscription \"Perbadanan\nKemajuan Filem Nasional Malaysia\" may be used as\na common seal.\n\n(2) All deeds, documents and other instruments\nrequiring the seal of the Perbadanan shall be sealed\naccordingly in the presence of two members of the\nPerbadanan who shall sign every deed, document or\ninstrument to which the seal is affixed; and such signing\nshall without further attestation be sufficient evidence\nthat the seal was duly and properly affixed and that\nthe same is the lawful seal of the Perbadanan:\n\n. Provided that a deed, document or other instrument\nwhich if executed by a person not being a body\ncorporate would not be required to be under seal may\nin like manner be executed by the Perbadanan; and\nsuch deed, document or instrument may be executed\non behalf of the Perbadanan by any of its officers or\nservants generally or specially authorised in writing so\nto act.                 |\n\n(3) The seal of the Perbadanan shall be officially\nand judicially noticed.\n\nPontian   6. (1) The functions of the Perbadanan shall be—\n\nPerbadanan.     (a) to make recommendations to the Minister as\n\nto the policies, methods and measures to be\nadopted to promote, nurture and facilitate the\ndevelopment of the film industry;\n\n(b) to develop, and stimulate the growth and\nmaintain the standards of, the film industry by\nvarious means, including the provision of\nresearch and advisory services;\n\n(c) to regulate and co-ordinate the activities of\npersons and bodies relating to matters pertain-\ning to the film industry;\n\n(2) generally to promote and assist, both inside\nand outside Malaysia, in the development of\nthe film industry;\n\n(Pt. II, S. 6]\n\nPERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM          9\nNASIONAL MALAYSIA\n\n(e) to regulate and control the production, distri-\nbution and exhibition of films in Malaysia, and\nin relation thereto to provide for the issue of\nlicences; and\n\n(f) to manage and control the maintenance and\noperation of places and equipment belonging\nto the Perbadanan for the purposes of sub-\nsection (2) (c).\n\n(2) The Perbadanan shall have power to do all things\nexpedient or reasonably necessary for or incidental to\nthe discharge of its functions and in particular, but\nwithout prejudice to the generality of the foregoing,\nit shall have the power—                            ;\n\n(a) to conduct surveys in respect of the film\nindustry and carry out feasibility studies. for\nthe development of film production locally;\n\n(b) to provide training facilities and to contro] and\nsupervise the implementation of training pro-\njects and programmes relating to the film\nindustry;\n\n(c) to provide or assist in the production of services,\nfacilities and filming equipment to film pro-\nducers, distributors and exhibitors and cinema-\nhall owners, but not itself to participate in film\nproduction, directly or indirectly;\n\n(d) to receive, in consideration of the services\nrendered by it, such commission or payment as\nmay be agreed upon;\n\n(e) to grant any subsidy or credit facility but in no\nway as to enable itself to participate in film\nproduction, directly or indirectly;\n\n(f) to prescribe and levy fees or other charges in\nrelation to the performance of its functions and\nthe exercise of its powers under this Act;\n\n(g) to participate in international organisations\nrelating to the film industry and to hold, pro-\nmote and participate in film festivals, exhibi-\ntions and seminars or in any activity of a similar\nnature both inside and outside Malaysia:\n\n(Pt. D-00, S. 6-9)\n\nDelegation.\n\nDirections\nby the\n\\                     Minister.\n\nAppoint-\nment of\nchief\nexecutive\nofficer\nand other\nofficers\nof the\n\nPerbadanan.\n\n10                                       Act 244\n\n(h) to establish institutions, centres, sub-centres\nand workshops for the undertaking of research\nand other activities necessary for or related to\nthe development of the film industry;\n\n(i) to provide incentives in respect of the film\nindustry;\n\n(j) to disseminate information to the public on the\nvarious aspects of the film industry; and\n\n(k) to do such other matters as may be directed by\nthe Minister."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"chapter":{"en":"ParT I"},"text":{"en":"7. (1) The Perbadanan may delegate any of its func-\ntions and powers to the Chairman.\n\n(2) Without prejudice to subsection (1), the Perba-\ndanan may, by an instrument in writing under its com-\nmon seal, delegate to any other person or any body\nsuch of its functions and powers as may be necessary\n\njo be performed inside of, outside Malaysiaf Are Thi\n\nProvided that any such person or body shall not have\ncontrol over the Fund and shall act in all respects in\naccordance with the directions of the Perbadanan."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"chapter":{"en":"ParT I"},"text":{"en":"8. (1) The Minister may give to the Perbadanan any\ndirection not inconsistent with the provisions of this\nAct as to the exercise and performance of its functions\nand powers in relation to any matter which appears to\nhim to concern the film industry and the Perbadanan\nshall give effect to any such direction.\n\n(2) The Perbadanan shall furnish the Minister with\nsuch information with respect to its property and activi-\nties as he may from time to time require.\n\nPART III\nADMINISTRATION"}},{"id":"MY-H215-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"9. (1) The Perbadanan may appoint a chief executive\nofficer who may be designated by any name, and such\nother officers and servants as it considers necessary for\nthe la of this Act and for the efficient conduct of\nits affairs.\n\n(2) The appointment of the chief executive officer\nshall be with the prior approval of the Minister and the\nname by which he is designated shall be published in\nthe Gazette.\n\npi\n\n(Pt. Ml, S. 9-13]\n\nPERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM         11\nNASIONAL MALAYSIA\n\n(3) If during any period the chief executive officer is\nfor any reason unable to exercise the powers and\nperform the duties of his office, the Perbadanan may,\nwith the prior approval of the Minister, appoint any\nother fit and proper person to so act."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"10. The chief executive officer shall—\n\n(a) be responsible for putting into execution the\npolicy decisions of the Perbadanan;\n\n(b) exercise supervision and control over all the\nother officers and servants of the Perbadanan;\nand\n\n(c) perform such duties and exercise such powers\n\nDuties of\nchief _\nexecutive\nofficer.\n\nas may from time to time be determined or- .\n\ndelegated by the Perbadanan or as the Chair-\nman may direct."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"11. (1) The officers and servants of the Perbadanan\n\nshall hold office for such period, receive such remunera- '\n\ntion, fees and allowances, and be subject to such\nconditions of service as may be determined by the\nPerbadanan with the approval of the Minister.\n\n(2) The Perbadanan shall have power to formulate\nand regulate the procedure for the appointment and\ndisciplining of its officers and servants.\n\n* 12. The members, officers and servants of the Per-\n| badanan and the members of a committee thereof shall\n\nbe deemed to be public servants within the meaning of\nthe Penal Code."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"13. (1) The Perbadanan may appoint such committees\nas it thinks desirable to exercise such functions and\npowers as may be delegated to them by the Perbadanan\nor to examine and report to the Perbadanan on any\nmatter arising out of or connected with any of the\nfunctions and powers of the Perbadanan under this\nAct.\n\n(2) A committee may do all such things as may be\nnecessary for the effective discharge of the functions\nand powers so delegated but shall be subject to the\ndirections of the Perbadanan.\n\nPerbadanan\n\nOo\ndetermine\nconditions\nof service\nof its\nofficers and\nservants.\n\nPublic\nservants For\npurposes o\nPenal Code.\nF.M S.\nCap. 45.\n\nCommittees.\n\n(Pt. III, S. 13-14]\n\nNo person\nhaving\ninterest\ntobe\nappointed\nas member,\nofficer or\nservant of\n\nthe\nPerbadanan.\n\n12                                     Act 244\n\n(3) A committee shall consist of a chairman and not\nmore than five other members who may be paid such\nremuneration or allowances as may be determined by\nthe Perbadanan with the approval of the Minister.\n\n(4) The provisions of the Schedule shall mutatis\nmutandis apply in respect of a committee appointed\nunder this section."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"14. (1) No person shall be appointed as a member, an\nofficer or a servant of the Perbadanan or as a member\nof a committee thereof if he has any interest, directly\nor indirectly, in—\n\n(a) any person, body, corporation or company\ncarrying on or engaged in, or about to carry\non or engage in, any of the activities or\" any\ncombination thereof referred to in section 21;\nor\n\n(b) any person, body, corporation or company with\nwhich the Perbadanan proposes to enter into\na contract or has entered into a subsisting\ncontract.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding subsection (1) (b), such person\nmay be appointed as a member, an officer or a servant\nof the Perbadanan or as a member of a committee\nthereof if he has an interest, directly or indirectly, as a\nshareholder only of a company referred to in that\nsubsection and provided that the holding of the shares\nin that company does not result in any controlling\ninterest, directly or indirectly.\n\n(3) Prior to his being appointed as a member, an\nofficer or servant of the Perbadanan or as a member\nof a committee thereof, every person shall disclose fully,\nin the case of a person who is to be appointed as a\nmember of the Perbadanan, to the Minister, and, in the\ncase of a person who is to be appointed as a member of\na committee or as an officer or a servant of the Per-\nbadanan, to the Perbadanan, whether he has any such\ninterest as is referred to in subsection (1).\n\n(4) Where such member, officer or servant acquires\nany such interest after the coming into operation of this\nAct, he shall cease to be such member, officer or servant\n\n\\\nSe ltyres\n\nPEP CALE RI In 21 oy ea   Fd 4\nGree ia Poe oe saa ke\n\n*«\n>\n\n¥\n»\n\nos\n\nEF ee Ln\naran\nnn\n\nDAR\n\na\n‘\n\nSeep mes 5\n=o\nhd\n\n\"Ss\na\n\n(Pt. III, S. 14-15]\n\nPERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM         13\nNASIONAL MALAYSIA\n\nof the Perbadanan or a committee thereof, as the case\nmay be, and his appointment shall be deemed to be\nrevoked forthwith:\n\na,\n\nA              Provided that this subsection shall not apply where\nthe member, officer or servant inherits or is bequeathed\nwith such interest and he relinquishes or disposes of such\ninterest within a period of three months of its being\nbequeathed and vesting in him and within that period\nreports in writing, in the case of a member of the\n\n|         Perbadanan, to the Minister and, in the case of a\n\n>           member of a committee or an officer or a servant, to\n\n         the Perbadanan, ‘the fact of such relinquishment or\ndisposal.\n\n(5) For the purposes of this section, \"indirect interest\"      /\nshall include the having or acquiring of any such\ninterest as is referred to in this section by a spouse or\na natural or an adopted child (below twenty-one years\nof age) of a person or a member, an officer or a servant\nof the Perbadanan or a member of a committee thereof,\nas the case may be.\n\n(6) Any person who contravenes any of the provisions\nof this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall, on\nconviction, be liable to imprisonment for a term not\nexceeding five years or to a fine not exceeding twenty-\nfive thousand ringgit or to both such imprisonment and\nfine.\n\nwy\n\nNN\ng          \"15. (1) A member of the Perbadanan or of a committee Declaration\n=        thereof who has or acquires, directly or indirectly, by interest and\n\n:       .               —                    disqualifi-\nhimself, his partner or agent                     ee kang\n\n(a) any share or interest—\n\n(i) in a contract or an arrangement made\nwith the Perbadanan;\n\n(ii) in any work to be done for the Perba-\ndanan; or\n\n(iii) in a company, firm or an undertaking\nwith which the Perbadanan proposes to\nenter into a contract or an agreement;\n\nPi Sgn vs\nfoe Wee,\nNiet has?\n\nor\n\neS\n%\n\n(Pt. UM, S. 15)\n\n14                                    Acr 244\n\n(b) any beneficial interest in immovable property\nproposed to be purchased or otherwise acquired\nor leased or otherwise dealt with by the\nPerbadanan,\n\nshall declare the nature and extent of his share or\ninterest to the Perbadanan or committee, as the case\nmay be.\n\n(2) The declaration required to be made by a mem-\nber under subsection (1) shall be made at the meeting\nof the Perbadanan or committee at which any question\nrelating to such contract, arrangement, work, purchase\nor other acquisition or lease or other dealing is first\ntaken into consideration or at the earliest opportunity\nafter the acquisition of such share or interest.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, a notice given\nto the other members by a member to the effect that\nhe has such share or interest as is specified in sub-\nsection (1) and is to bé regarded as interested in any\nsuch contract, arrangement, work, purchase or other\nacquisition or lease or other dealing which may, after\nthe date of the notice, be made with, or be required\nto be carried out by, the company, firm or undertaking\nin question shall be deemed to be sufficient declaration\nof interest in relation thereto:\n\nProvided that such notice shall be of no effect unless\nit is given at a meeting of the Perbadanan or-committee\nor the member concerned takes all reasonable steps to\nensure that it is brought up and read at the next meet-\ning of the Perbadanan or committee after it is given.\n\n(4) Every declaration made in pursuance of this\nsection shall be recorded in the minutes of the\nmeeting at which it is made or read and shall have no\neffect until it is so recorded.        |\n\n(5) A member shall not vote upon any resolution\nor question relating to any such contract, arrangement,\nwork, purchase or other acquisition, or lease or other\ndealing in which he has any share or interest whether\nor not he has declared the same, nor shall he take\npart in any deliberation (except on the invitation of\nthe Perbadanan or committee) or decision relating\nthereto or to any matter incidental thereto, and if he\n\n(Pt. III-IV, S. 15-16)\n\nPERBADANAN KBMAJUAN FILEM         15\nNASIONAL MALAYSIA\n\nshall do so his vote shall not be counted, nor shall he\nbe counted in the quorum present at the meeting for\nthe purposes of such resolution or question.\n\n(6) A member shall not be deemed to have a share\nor interest under this section by reason only of his\nbeing a shareholder in the company with which it is\nproposed that the Perbadanan shall enter into a con-\ntract or an arrangement unless he has a controlling\ninterest in that company.\n\n(7) A member who contravenes any of the provisions\nof this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall,\non conviction, be liable to imprisonment for a term not\nexceeding five years or to a fine not exceeding twenty-\nfive thousand ringgit or to both such imprisonment and\nfine.\n\nPART IV\nFINANCE"}},{"id":"MY-H215-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"16. For the purposes of this Act there is established\na fund, which in this Act is referred to as \"the Fund\",\nto be administered and controlled by the Perbadanan—\n\n(a) into which shall be paid—\n\n(i) such sums as may be provided from time\nto time by Parliament;\n\n(ii) such sums as may from time to time be\nborrowed by the Perbadanan for the\npurpose of meeting any of its obligations\nor discharging any of its functions and\npowers;\n\n(iii) all moneys earned by the Perbadanan;\n\n(iv) all moneys earned or arising from any\nproperty, investment, mortgage, charge\nor debenture acquired by or vested in the\nPerbadanan;\n\n(v) any fees or other charges prescribed and\ncollected by the Perbadanan; and\n\n(vi) all other sums or property which may in\nany manner become payable to or vested\nin the Perbadanan in respect of any matter\nincidental to its functions and powers;\n\nThe Fund\nof the\n\nPerbadanan.\n\n|Pt. IV, S. 16-20)\n\nBorrowing\npowers.\n\nInvestment.\n\nFinance.\n\nStatutory\nBodies\n(Accounts\nand Annual\nReports)\nAct 1980.\nAct 240.\n\n16                                 Act 244\n\n(6) and out of which shall be defrayed—\n\n(i) all expenditure, including capital expen-\nditure, incurred by the Perbadanan in\ncarrying out its functions and duties;\n\n(ii) moneys for the repayment of any loan\nmade to the Perbadanan pursuant to its\npower to borrow; and\n\n(ili) any subsidy or credit facility granted by\nthe Perbadanan pursuant to its powers\nunder this Act."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"17. The Perbadanan may, with the approval of the\nMinister of Finance and upon such terms and condi-\ntions as may be determined by him, borrow such sums\nas it may require for discharging any 'of its functions\nand powers under this Act."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"18. The Fund of the Perbadanan shall, in so far as'it\nis not required to be expended by the Perbadanan under\nthis Act, be invested in such manner as the Minister of\nFinance may approve.\n\n19, (1) The expenses of the Perbadanan up to such\namount as may be authorised by the Minister for any\none year shall be defrayed out of the Fund.\n\n(2) Before the beginning of September of each year,\nthe Perbadanan shall submit to the Minister an estimate\n\n‘of the expenses for the following year in such form and\n\nwith such particulars as the Minister may require; and\nthe Minister shall, before the beginning of November\nof that year, notify the Perbadanan of the amount\nauthorised for expenses generally or of the amount\nauthorised for each description of expenditure.\n\n(3) The Perbadanan may, at any time, submit to the\nMinister a supplementary estimate for any one year\nand the Minister may allow the whole or any part of\nthe additional expenditure included therein."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20"},"chapter":{"en":"PART IV"},"text":{"en":"20. The Statutory Bodies (Accounts and Annual\nReports) Act 1980 shall apply in respect of the\nPerbadanan.\n\n(Pt. V, S. 21-23)\n\nPERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM         17\nNASIONAL MALAYSIA\n\nPART V\nPRODUCTION, DISTRIBUTION AND EXHIBITION\nOF FILMS"}},{"id":"MY-H215-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"21. (1) Subject to the provisions of this Part, no person\nshall engage in all three activities of production, distri-\nbution and exhibition of films but he may, however:\nengage in any one of the following combinations of\nactivities—\n\n(a) production and distribution; or\n\n(b) production and exhibition; or\n\n‘(c) distribution and exhibition,\nof films. —                             €\n\n(2) Subsection (1) shall not in any way be construed\nas preventing a person from engaging in only oné of\nthe activities of production, distribution or exhibition\nof films."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"22. (1) No person shall engage in any of the activities\nof production, distribution or exhibition of films or any\ncombination of those activities as specified in section 21\n(1) unless there is in force a licence authorising him to\ndo the same.\n\n(2) An application for a licence shall be made on the\nprescribed form to the Perbadanan, and the licence may\nbe issued on payment of the prescribed fees for the\nprescribed period and subject to such terms and\nconditions as may be imposed therein.\n\n(3) The Perbadanan may refuse to issue a licence\nwithout assigning any reason therefor or it may issue a\nlicence subject to terms and conditions, and its decision\nin any case shall be final and conclusive and shall not be\nchallenged, appealed against, reviewed, quashed or\nquestioned in any court.                     |\n=D A"}},{"id":"MY-H215-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"23. (1) No partnership of which a person licensed under\nsection 22 is a partner, and no company in which such\nperson has a controlling interest, directly or indirectly,\nshall engage in any of the activities of production,\ndistribution or exhibition of films:\n\nNo person\n\nto engage\n\nin al] three\nactivities of\nproduction,\ndistribution       |\n\nan\nexhibition\nof films. '\n\nActivity or\ncombination\nof activities\n\nto be\nlicensed.\n\nIns PraS OK\n\nc— As\n\nRestriction\non partner-\nship or\ncompany\nwhere ‘\nperson has\ncontrolling\ninterest.\n\n(Pt. V, S. 23-25)\n\n}              Person\n:           licensed to\nascertain\n\n18                             Act 244\n\nProvided that where such person engages in only one\nof the activities of production, distribution or exhibi-\ntion of films, the partnership or company may engage\nin the other only of the combination of activities\nreferred to in section 21 (1).\n\n(2) For the purposes of this section, \"indirect\ninterest\" shall include the having or acquiring of an\ninterest in a partnership or company by a spouse or a\nnatural or an adopted child (below twenty-one years of\nage) of such person and, where such person is a com-\npany, by any member of the board of directors of the\ncompany or a spouse or a natural or an adopted child\n(below twenty-one years of age) of such member."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"24. (1) A person licensed under section 22 shall not\nengage in any one of the activities or the combination\n\n,  thatfilmhas thereof referred to in section 21 without first ascer-\n\ncome into\n\ntaining that any film which is the subject-matter of his\n\nossession,\ncustody or activity or combination of activities has come into the\n      one.     possession, custody or control of himself, his servant or\nagent lawfully.\n|            (2) In any prosecution for an offence under this\nsection, it shall be presumed that the film came into\nthe possession, custody or control of such person, his\nservant or agent unlawfully unless such person is able\nto prove that the film so came into possession, custody\n!             or control without his knowledge, consent or conni-\nvance or that of his servant or agent and that he\nexercised all due diligence to prevent the film so coming\nIns PPS        into possession, custody or control.\nOffenceto 25, (1) Any person who contravenes any of the provi-\ncet\" sions of this Part shall be guilty of an offence and shall,\n\"     provisions On conviction, be liable to a fine not exceeding fifty\n\nthousand ringgit/and he shall in addition, in the case of\na continuing offence, be liable to daily fine not\nexceeding ten thousand ringgitf\n\n(2) Where a person who has been issued with a\nlicénce under section 22 is guilty of an offence, the\nlicence shall be liable to be cancelled by the Perbadanan\nand the provisions of section 22 (3) shall apply in respect\nof any decision of the Perbadanan to cancel the licence.\n\nsr\n\n[Pt. V-VI, S. 26-29]\n\nPERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM        19\nNASIONAL MALAYSIA"}},{"id":"MY-H215-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"26. Where an offence under this Part is committed by Persons who\na company or a firm, every director, secretary or mana- Shallbe\nger of the company or, as the case may be, every be guilty\npartner in the firm shall also be deemed to be guilty of f*\"**\nthe offence unless he proves that the offence was com-\n\nmitted without his knowledge, consent or connivance\n\nand that he exercised all due diligence to prevent the\ncommission of the offence.\n\nPART uk                        c— ass\naii          Part VI             Iny MBI\nMISCELLANEOUS"}},{"id":"MY-H215-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"27. (1) No action, suit, prosecution or other proceed- Protection\nings shall be brought or instituted personally against sinstiren!\nany member of the Perbadanan or a committee thereof\n\nor against an officer or a servant of the Perbadanan in\n\nrespect of any act done, omission committed or state-\n\nment made bona fide in pursuance or execution or\nintended execution of the provisions of this Act.\n\n(2) Where any person is exempted from liability by\nreason only of the provisions of this section, the Per-\nbadanan shall be liable only to the extent that it would\nbe if such person were a member, an Officer, or a\nservant or an agent of the Perbadanan or a member\nof a committee thereof."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"28. Notwithstanding the provisions of any written law Appearance\nto the contrary, in civil proceedings by or against the P499.\nPerbadanan, any person holding the appointment of of civil .\nfederal counsel and authorised by the Attorney General procerdines\nin that behalf may, on behalf of the Perbadanan, counsel.\ninstitute, appear in and conduct such proceedings and\ndo all other matters, acts and. obligations in respect of\n\nsuch proceedings."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"29. (1) Except for the purposes of the Government as Information\nmay be necessary from time to time, of any law or of of oreanisa-\nperforming his duties, no person, or member, officer business,\n\nor servant of the Perbadanan or member of a committee finance...\nthereof shall disclose any information concerning the and affairs\n\nOrganisation, business, finance, transactions or affairs pa...\nof the Perbadanan or any of its committees.           not to be\ndisclosed\"\n(2) Any person or member, officer or servant who except in\nKnowingly contravenes any of the provisions of sub- \"eriain\nsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence and shall, on stances.\n\n(Pt. VI, S. 29-32]\n\nCourts\nwhich have\njurisdiction\nto try\noffences.\n\nBAG\n\nAll offences\nunder Act\ndeemed to\nbe seizable.\nF.M.S.\nCap. 6.\n\nValidation\nof acts\ndone in\nanticipation\nof Act.\n\n20                                     Act 244\n\nconviction, be liable to imprisonment for a term not\nexceeding two years or to a fine not exceeding five\nthousand ringgit or to both such imprisonment and fine."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"30. (1) Notwithstanding the provisions of any written\nlaw to the contrary, a Sessions Court or, in the State\nof Sabah or Sarawak, the Court of a Magistrate of the\nFirst Class shall have jurisdiction to try any offence\nunder this Act or subsidiaryjlegislation made thereunder\nand impose the full penalty provided therefor.\n\n(2) The Court trying any person accused of an\noffence under this Act or gubsidiary legislation made\nthereunder may at the condlusion of the trial, whether\nthe alleged offender is convitted or not, order that any\nfilm produced as an exhibit} before the Court shall be\ndestroyed or otherwise dealt with as the Court thinks\nfit."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"31. Any offence alleged to|\\be committed under this\nAct or subsidiary legislation made thereunder' shall be\ndeemed to be a seizable offence for the purposes of the\nCriminal Procedure Code and a police officer may\nexercise in respect of such | bffence any or all of the\npowers that a police officer|may exercise in respect of\na seizable offence under that! Code."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A32","no":32,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 32"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"32. (1) All acts and things done by any person or\nauthority, whether or not purporting to be done for or\non behalf of the Perbadanan, in anticipation for or in\nanticipation of the promulgation of this Act and any\nexpenditure incurred in relation thereto shall be deemed\nto have been authorised by this Act provided that the\nacts and things done are not inconsistent with the\ngeneral intention and purposes of this Act, and the\nrights and obligations acquired or incurred as a result\nof the doing of acts and things or any expenditure so\nincurred shall be deemed to be the rights and obliga-\ntions of the Perbadanan.\n\n(2) For the avoidance of doubt, it is declared that\nsubsection (1) does not authorise the appointment of\nmembers, officers or servants of the Perbadanan except\nin so far as authorising the temporary appointment of\nsuch persons until appointed under this Act.\n\n©)!\n\n(Pt. VI, S. 33-34, Schedule]\n\nPERBADANAN KEMAJUAN FILEM         21\nNASIONAL MALAYSIA"}},{"id":"MY-H215-A33","no":33,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 33"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"33. Nothing in this Act shall derogate from the provi-\nsions of any other written law relating to films or to\n\nentertainment."}},{"id":"MY-H215-A34","no":34,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 34"},"chapter":{"en":"PART V"},"text":{"en":"34. (1) The Perbadanan may, with the approval of the\nMinister, make such regulations as it may deem expe-\ndient or necessary to carry out the purposes and pro-\nvisions of this Act and for the discharge of its functions\n\nand the exercise of its powers.\n\n(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the fore-\ngoing, the Perbadanan may, with the approval of the\nMinister, in particular make regulations in respect of\nthe following matters—\n\n(a) to regulate by licensing any film activity, to\nprovide for terms and conditions to be imposed\non licences, and for fees, charges and deposits\nin respect thereof, including provisions for the\nforfeiture, use or return of such deposits and\nfor offences under the regulations to be\npunished in like manner as offences under this\nAct;\n\n(b) to prescribe forms and all other matters neces-\nsary for the purposes of Part V; -amd\n\n(c) to regulate the provision of research, training\nand instruction in respect of any film activity\nand for the Perbadanan to itself establish\n\n,,) institutions or provide facilities for the same;\n\nSCHEDULE\n(Section 4 (4))\n1. The following persons shall be disqualified for being appointed\nor being members of the Perbadanan—\n(a) a person who is of unsound mind or is otherwise incapable\n—— A          of performing his duty;\n(b) a bankrupt;\n\n(c)a person who has been convicted of an offence and\nsentenced to imprisonment for a term of one year or more.\n\n_BUA..\n34)...\n\n2. A member of the Perbadanan shall be deemed to have vacated\nhis office if he is absent from three consecutive meetings of the\nPerbadanan without the prior approval in writing of the Minister.\n\nAct not to\nderogate\nfrom other\nlaws.\n\nRegulations.\n\n(ny\n\nappointed\nmembers of the\nPerbadanan.\n\nMember\n\napproval of\nMinister.\n\nChairman and\nthreo othor\nmembers to\nform quorum\n\nof tho\nPerbadanan.\n\nChairman to\nhavo casting\nvote,\n\nPerbadanan to\ndetermine ils\nprocedure.\n\nPerbadanan\nmay appoint\ncommittees,\n\n22                               Acr 244\n\n3. (1) The Chairman, or any member presiding in the absence of\nthe Chairman, and three other members shall form a quorum at a\nmeeting of the Perbadanan.\n\n(2) In the absence of the Chairman the Deputy Chairman shall\npreside at a meeting of the Perbadanan and, in the absence of\nboth of them, the members present shall choose one of their\nnumber to preside and such member may exercise all the powers\nof the Chairman in respect of that meeting.\n\n4. If on any question to be determined there is an equality of\nvotes the Chairman shall have the casting vote in addition to his\ndeliberative vote.\n\n5. Subject to this Act, the Perbadanan shall determine its own\nprocedure.\n\n6. (1) The Perbadanan may appoint such committees of its\nmembers with or without other persons as it may determine.\n\n(2) Any committee so appointed shall conform to instructions\nthat may from time to time be given to it by the Perbadanan,\nand the Perbadanan may at any time discontinue or alter the\nconstitution of such committee.\n\n(3) Subject to the directions of the Perbadanan, the quorum and\nprocedure of a committee shall be determined by. the committee.\n\nKUALA LUMPUR\nDICETAK OLEH PEMANGKU KETUA PENGARAH PERCETAKAN NEGARA DAN DITERBITKAN DENGAN\nPERINTAH PADA 1911p FEBRUARI 1981\n\nHarga: $1"}}],"pack":"my-5"};
  FT["MY-H2150"] = {"id":"MY-H2150","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 190/2025&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2025年娱乐税（豁免）（第23号）令","en":"ENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 23) ORDER 2025","orig":"ENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 23) ORDER 2025","ms":"Perintah Duti Hiburan (Pengecualian) (Bilangan 23) 2025","vi":"Lệnh về Thuế giải trí (Miễn trừ) (số 23) năm 2025","th":"คำสั่งภาษีบันเทิง (การยกเว้น) (ฉบับที่ 23) ค.ศ. 2025","id":"Perintah Bea Hiburan (Pembebasan) (Nomor 23) Tahun 2025"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA190","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2025","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2025_P.U.(A)190-2025_ENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 23) ORDER 2025.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H2150-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Duti Hiburan (Pengecualian)\n\n(No. 23) 2025.\n\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H2150-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Menteri mengecualikan enam puluh peratus daripada duti hiburan yang\n\nkena dibayar atas tiket masuk bagi persembahan ILLAIYARAAJA \"RAJA RHAPSODY\n\nMAESTRO LIVE IN CONCERT\" yang telah diadakan di Stadium Hoki Nasional, Bukit Jalil,\n\nKuala Lumpur pada 5 April 2025.\n\nDibuat 16 Jun 2025\n\n[MOF.700-4/6/40; PN(PU2)174/JLD.13]\n\nDATUK SERI AMIR HAMZAH AZIZAN\n\nMenteri Kewangan II\n\nENTERTAINMENTS DUTY ACT 1953\n\nENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 23) ORDER 2025\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 12(1)(b) of the\n\nEntertainments Duty Act 1953 [Act 103], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-5"};
  FT["MY-H2151"] = {"id":"MY-H2151","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 190/2026&status=CANCEL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2026年印刷机与出版物（不良出版物管制）（废止）令","en":"PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (REVOCATION) ORDER 2026","orig":"PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (REVOCATION) ORDER 2026","vi":"Lệnh về Máy in và ấn phẩm (Kiểm soát ấn phẩm không mong muốn) (Bãi bỏ) năm 2026","th":"คำสั่งแท่นพิมพ์และสิ่งพิมพ์ (การควบคุมสิ่งพิมพ์ที่ไม่พึงประสงค์) (การเพิกถอน) ค.ศ. 2026","id":"Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan (Pengendalian Terbitan Tidak Diinginkan) (Pencabutan) Tahun 2026","ms":"Perintah Mesin Cetak dan Penerbitan (Kawalan Penerbitan Tidak Diingini) (Pembatalan) 2026"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA190","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2026","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2026_P.U.(A)190-2026_PRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS (CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (REVOCATION) ORDER 2026.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H2151-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"1. Wacana Pemikiran Reformis (Jilid I)"}},{"id":"MY-H2151-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"2. Wacana Pemikiran Reformis (Jilid II)\n\nDibuat 30 April 2026\n\n[KDN.PK.S.600-1/3/64; PN(PU2)417/JLD.28]\n\n DATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\n Menteri Dalam Negeri\n\nPRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS ACT 1984\n\nPRINTING PRESSES AND PUBLICATIONS\n\n(CONTROL OF UNDESIRABLE PUBLICATIONS) (REVOCATION) ORDER 2026\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 7(1) of the Printing Presses\n\nand Publications Act 1984 [Act 301], the Minister revokes the Printing Presses\n\nand Publications (Control of Undesirable Publications) (No. 32) Order 2017\n\n[P.U. (A) 283/2017] which has been published in the Gazette on 28 September 2017\n\nwhich prohibited the printing, importation, production, reproduction, publishing,\n\nsale, issue, circulation, distribution or possession of publications specified\n\nin the Schedule.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\n1. Wacana Pemikiran Reformis (Jilid I)\n\n2. Wacana Pemikiran Reformis (Jilid II)\n\nMade 30 April 2026\n\n[KDN.PK.S.600-1/3/64; PN(PU2)417/JLD.28]\n\n DATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\n Minister of Home Affairs"}}],"pack":"my-5"};
  FT["MY-H2152"] = {"id":"MY-H2152","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 191/2011&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2011年关税（计价）（棕榈油）（第24号）令","en":"CUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 24) ORDER 2011","orig":"CUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 24) ORDER 2011","ms":"Perintah Kastam (Nilai) (Minyak Sawit) (Bilangan 24) 2011","vi":"Lệnh về Hải quan (Trị giá) (Dầu cọ) (số 24) năm 2011","th":"คำสั่งศุลกากร (มูลค่า) (น้ำมันปาล์ม) (ฉบับที่ 24) ค.ศ. 2011","id":"Perintah Kepabeanan (Nilai) (Minyak Kelapa Sawit) (Nomor 24) Tahun 2011"},"level":"regulation","category":"03_涉外投资与贸易","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA191","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2011","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\03_涉外投资与贸易\\2011_P.U.(A)191-2011_CUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 24) ORDER 2011.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H2152-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Kastam (Nilai -Nilai) (Minyak\nKelapa Sawit) (No. 24 ) 2011 dan hendaklah mula berkuat  kuasa bagi tempoh dari\n13 Jun 2011 hingga 19 Jun 2011.\n\nPemungutan dan pembayaran duti kastam"}},{"id":"MY-H2152-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Bagi maksud pemungutan dan pembayaran duti -duti kastam, menurut\nperuntukan-peruntukan Perintah Duti Kastam 2007 [ P.U. (A) 441/2007], nilai bagi tiap -\ntiap s atu barang berduti yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (1) dan (2) Jadual mengikut\nunitnya yang tersebut dalam ruang (3) hendaklah nilai yang dinyatakan dalam ruang\n(4).\n\nCUSTOMS ACT 1967\n\nCUSTOMS (VALUES) (PALM OIL) (NO. 24) ORDER 2011\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 12 of the Customs Act 1967 [Act 235], the\nMinister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\nJADUAL / SCHEDULE\nBarang\n(Goods)\n(1)\n\nSubkepala\n(Subheading)\n(2)\nUnit\n(Unit)\n(3)\nNilai\n(Value)\n(4)\nCrude Palm Oil 1511.10 100 tonne RM3,417.45\n\nDibuat 10 Jun 2011\nMade 10 June 2011\n[KE.HT(94)819/03-6/KLT. 10(30); Perb.(8.20)116/1-4; PN(PU2)338/XXVIII]\n\n          Dengan arahan Menteri Kewangan/\n          By direction of the Minister of Finance\n\n    Bagi pihak dan atas nama Menteri Kewangan/\n          On behalf and in the name of the Minister of Finance\n\n DATO' SITI HALIMAH BINTI ISMAIL\n Setiausaha/Secretary\nBahagian Analisa Cukai/\nTax Analysis Division"}}],"pack":"my-5"};
  FT["MY-H2153"] = {"id":"MY-H2153","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 191/2012&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2012年选举（选举进行）（修正）（第3号）条例","en":"ELECTIONS (CONDUCT OF ELECTIONS)(AMENDMENT) (NO. 3) REGULATIONS 2012","orig":"ELECTIONS (CONDUCT OF ELECTIONS)(AMENDMENT) (NO. 3) REGULATIONS 2012","ms":"Peraturan Pilihan Raya (Pengendalian Pilihan Raya) (Pindaan) (Bilangan 3) 2012","vi":"Quy định về Bầu cử (Tiến hành bầu cử) (Sửa đổi) (số 3) năm 2012","th":"ข้อบังคับการเลือกตั้ง (การดำเนินการเลือกตั้ง) (การแก้ไข) (ฉบับที่ 3) ค.ศ. 2012","id":"Peraturan Pemilihan Umum (Penyelenggaraan Pemilihan Umum) (Perubahan) (Nomor 3) Tahun 2012"},"level":"regulation","category":"01_宪法与基础法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA191","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2012","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\01_宪法与基础法\\2012_P.U.(A)191-2012_ELECTIONS (CONDUCT OF ELECTIONS)(AMENDMENT) (NO. 3) REGULATIONS 2012.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H2153-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan\nPilihan Raya (Penjalanan Pilihan Raya) (Pindaan) (No. 3) 2012.\n(2) Peraturan-Peraturan ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 25 Jun 2012.\nPindaan peraturan 19A"}},{"id":"MY-H2153-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Peraturan-Peraturan Pilihan Raya (Penjalanan Pilihan Raya) 1981\n[P.U. (A) 386/1981] dipinda dalam subperaturan 19A(2) dalam teks bahasa kebangsaan\ndengan memasukkan se belum perkataan \"hendaklah enggan\" perkataan \"atau mana -\nmana orang yang bertindak di bawah kuasanya\".\nDibuat 22 Jun 2012\n[SPR(R)107; PN(PU2)178E]\nDengan arahan Suruhanjaya Pilihan Raya\nDATUK KAMARUDDIN BIN MOHAMED BARIA\nSetiausaha\nSuruhanjaya Pilihan Raya\n[Akan dibentangkan dalam Dewan Rakyat menurut seksyen 17 Akta Pilihan Raya 1958]\n\nELECTIONS ACT 1958\nELECTIONS (CONDUCT OF ELECTIONS) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 3)\nREGULATIONS 2012\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 16 of the Elections Act 1958 [ Act 19], the\nElection Commission, with the approval of the Yang di -Pertuan Agong, makes the\nfollowing regulations:\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-5"};
