  FT["MY-H2228"] = {"id":"MY-H2228","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 195/2025&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2025年联邦道路（联邦土地发展局计划）（修正）（第2号）令","en":"FEDERAL ROADS (FELDA SCHEME) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 2) ORDER 2025","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (FELDA SCHEME) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 2) ORDER 2025","ms":"Perintah Jalan Raya Persekutuan (Rancangan FELDA) (Pindaan) (Bilangan 2) 2025","vi":"Lệnh về Đường bộ liên bang (Chương trình FELDA) (Sửa đổi) (số 2) năm 2025","th":"คำสั่งทางหลวงสหพันธ์ (โครงการ FELDA) (การแก้ไข) (ฉบับที่ 2) ค.ศ. 2025","id":"Perintah Jalan Raya Federal (Skema FELDA) (Perubahan) (Nomor 2) Tahun 2025"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA195","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2025","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 3 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2025_P.U.(A)195-2025_FEDERAL ROADS (FELDA SCHEME) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 2) ORDER 2025.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H2228-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Jalan Persekutuan\n\n(Skim Felda) (Pindaan) (No. 2) 2025.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 30 Jun 2025.\n\nPindaan Jadual Pertama"}},{"id":"MY-H2228-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Jalan Persekutuan (Skim Felda) 1991 [P.U. (A) 449/1991], yang disebut\n\n\"Perintah ibu\" dalam Perintah ini, dipinda dalam Jadual Pertama di bawah kepala\n\nNegeri Perlis—\n\n(a) berhubung dengan butiran Mata Air—\n\n(i) dalam ruang Jalan Masuk (km), dengan menggantikan perkataan\n\n\"2.750\" dengan perkataan \"1.364\"; dan\n\n(ii) dalam ruang Jalan Kampung (km), dengan menggantikan perkataan\n\n\"8.080\" dengan perkataan \"5.991\";\n\n(b) berhubung dengan butiran Rimba Mas—\n\n(i) dalam ruang Jalan Masuk (km), dengan menggantikan perkataan\n\n\"0.69\" dengan perkataan \"2.345\"; dan\n\n(ii) dalam ruang Jalan Kampung (km), dengan menggantikan perkataan\n\n\"6.26\" dengan perkataan \"5.110\"; dan\n\n\";\n\n(c) berhubung dengan butiran Chuping—\n\n(i) dalam ruang Jalan Masuk (km), dengan menggantikan perkataan\n\n\"6.354\" dengan perkataan \"6.376\"; dan\n\n(ii) dalam ruang Jalan Kampung (km), dengan menggantikan perkataan\n\n\"25.640\" dengan perkataan \"13.839\".\n\nPindaan Jadual Kedua"}},{"id":"MY-H2228-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Perintah ibu dipinda dalam Jadual Kedua—\n\n(a) dengan menggantikan PETA 21: MATA AIR dengan peta yang berikut:\n\n\"PETA 21: MATA AIR\n\n\"; dan\n\n(b) dengan menggantikan PETA 22: CHUPING dengan peta yang berikut:\n\n\"PETA 22: CHUPING\n\n\".\n\n(c) dengan memasukkan selepas PETA 31: KEMENDORE peta yang berikut:\n\n\"PETA 32: RIMBA MAS\n\nDibuat 20 Jun 2025\n\n[KKR.100-1/2/16; PN(PU2)391/JLD.52]\n\nDATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\nMenteri Kerja Raya\n\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut seksyen 4 Akta Jalan Persekutuan 1959]\n\nFEDERAL ROADS ACT 1959\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (FELDA SCHEME) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 2) ORDER 2025\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 3 of the Federal Roads Act 1959 [Act 376],\n\nthe Minister, after consultation with the State Government of Perlis,\n\nmakes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-5"};
  FT["MY-H2229"] = {"id":"MY-H2229","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 195/2026&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2026年娱乐税（豁免）（第23号）令","en":"ENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 23) ORDER 2026","orig":"ENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 23) ORDER 2026","ms":"Perintah Duti Hiburan (Pengecualian) (Bilangan 23) 2026","vi":"Lệnh về Thuế giải trí (Miễn trừ) (số 23) năm 2026","th":"คำสั่งภาษีบันเทิง (การยกเว้น) (ฉบับที่ 23) ค.ศ. 2026","id":"Perintah Bea Hiburan (Pembebasan) (Nomor 23) Tahun 2026"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA195","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2026","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2026_P.U.(A)195-2026_ENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 23) ORDER 2026.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H2229-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Duti Hiburan (Pengecualian)\n\n(No. 23) 2026.\n\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H2229-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Menteri mengecualikan tiket masuk bagi persembahan 林子祥 x 葉蒨文 白頭到老\n\nWE ARE ONE 世界巡迴演唱會 - 吉隆坡站 yang telah diadakan di Unifi Arena Bukit Jalil,\n\nKuala Lumpur pada 14 Mac 2026 daripada duti hiburan.\n\nDibuat 13 Mei 2026\n\n[MOF.700-4/6/45; PN(PU2)174/JLD.14]\n\nDATUK SERI AMIR HAMZAH BIN AZIZAN\n\nMenteri Kewangan II\n\nENTERTAINMENTS DUTY ACT 1953\n\nENTERTAINMENTS DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 23) ORDER 2026\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 12(1)(b)\n\nof the Entertainments Duty Act 1953 [Act 103], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-5"};
  FT["MY-H223"] = {"id":"MY-H223","coverage":"partial","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-detail.php?act=254&lang=BI","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":31,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"1953年时效法","en":"LIMITATION ACT 1953","orig":"LIMITATION ACT 1953","vi":"Luật về Thời hiệu năm 1953","th":"พระราชบัญญัติอายุความ ค.ศ. 1953","id":"Undang-Undang Daluwarsa Tahun 1953","ms":"Akta Had Masa 1953"},"level":"law","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"ACT254","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"1953","completenessNote":"全文：第 3 条至第 36 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。源文第 1—2 条无编号（扫描件边注数字缺失），未臆造条号。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\1953_254_LIMITATION ACT 1953.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H223-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"chapter":{"en":"Part I."},"text":{"en":"3. This Ordinance shall not apply to any action or Saving for\narbitration for which a period of limitation is othe .\nx                     .                       .    imitation\nprescribed by /any other written law or to any action enactments.\nden safi or arbitration to which 4he-Grewa-er the Government\n\nJenaka\n\nLimitation\nnot to\noperate as\na bar unless\nspecially\npleaded.\n\nPart II\nto be\nsubject to\nprovisions\n\nof Part III.\n\nLimitation\nof actions\nof contract\nand tort\nand certain\nother\nactions.\n\n24            Ne 4 oF 1953,\n\nor the Government of any State enm—Settlement is a\nparty and for which if it were between subjects a\nperiod of limitation would have been prescribed by\nany other written law."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II"},"text":{"en":"4. Nothing in this Ordinance shall operate as a bar\nto an action unless this Ordinance has been expressly\npleaded as a defence thereto/in any case where under\nany written law relating to civil procedure for the\ntime being in force such a defence is required to be\nso pleaded.\n\nPart II."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"5. The provisions of this Part shall have effect\nsubject to the provisions of Part III of this\nOrdinance.\n\nACTIONS OF CONTRACT JAND TORT AND CERTAIN\nOTHER /ACTIONS."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"6. (1) Save as hereinafter provided the following\nactions shall not be brought after the expiration of\nsix years from the date on which the cause of action\naccrued, that is to say—                     —     -\n\n(a) actions founded jon a contract or on tort;\n\n(0) actions to enfor¢e a recognisance;\n\n(c) actions to enfor¢e an award;\n\n(dz) actions to recdver any sum recoverable by\nvirtue of any written law other than a\npenalty or forfeiture or of a sum by way\nof penalty or forfeiture.\n\n_ (2) An action for an account shall not be brought\nin respect of any matter which arose more than six\nyears before the commencement of the action.\n\n(3) An action upon any judgment shall not be\nbrought after the expiration of twelve years from the\ndate on which the judgment became enforceable and\nno arrears of interest in respect of any judgment\ndebt shall be recovered after the expiration of six\nyears from the date on which the interest became due.\n\n(4) An action to fecover any penalty or forfeiture\nor sum by way of penalty or forfeiture recoverable by\nvirtue of any Ordinance or other written law shall\nnot be brought after the expiration of one year from\nthe date on which the cause of action accrued :\n\nProvided that for the purpose of this sub-section\nthe expression ‘‘penalty'' shall not include a fine to\nwhich a person is/ liable on conviction for a criminal\noffence.\n\nLIMITATION. ;                              25\n\n(5) Nothing in this section shall apply to—\n\n(a) any cause of action within the Admiralty\njurisdiction of the/High Court which is\nenforceable in rem/ other than an action\nto recover the wages of seamen, or\n\n(6) any action to recover money secured by any\nmortgage of or charge on land or personal\nproperty.\n\n(6) Subject to the provisions of sections 22 and 32\nof this Ordinance the provisions of this section shall\napply (if necessary by analogy) to all claims for\nspecific performance of a contract or for an injunction\nor for other equitable relief whether the same be\nfounded upon any contract or tort or upon any trust\nor other ground in equity."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"7. (1) Where any tani of action in respect of the\nconversion or wrongful detention of a chattel has\naccrued to any person and before he recovers possession\nof the chattel, a further conversion or wrongful\ndetention takes place, / no action shall be brought in\nrespect of the further conversion or detention after\nthe expiration of sia years from the accrual of the\ncause of action in respect of the original conversion\nor detention.\n\n(2) Where any ve cause of action has accrued to\nany person and the period prescribed for bringing\nthat action and foy bringing any action in respect of\nsuch a further conversion or wrongful detention as\naforesaid has expired and he has not during that\nperiod recovered possession of the chattel the title of\nthat person to the chattel shall be extinguished."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"8. An action\n\n(a) to set aside a sale in pursuance of the order\nof a/Collector or other officer of revenue;\n\n(D) to set aside a sale for arrears of Government,\n\nrevenue or for any\ndemand recoverable as such arrears;\n\n(c) to set} aside any attachment, lease or transfer\n\nof immovable property by the revenue\n\nauthorities for arrears of Government\nrevenue;\n\n(d) against the Government or the Government\nof any State or—Settlement to recover\nmoney paid under protest in satisfaction\n\nLimitation\nin case of\nsuccessive\nconversions\nand extinc-\ntion of title\nof owner\nof converted\ngoods.\n\nLimitation\nof certain\nactions in\nrespect of\nrevenue\nmatters.\n\nKor da.\nAM. 332/09\n\nKO. Mak\nLW. SYS\n\nLimitation\nof actions\nto recover\nland.\n\nS.S. Cap.\n\nS.S. Cap.\n\nS.S. Cap.\n\nNo. 57 of\n\nAccrual of\nright of\nclaim in\ncase of\npresent\ninterests\nin land.\n\n26            No. 4 oF 1953.\n\nof a claim made by the revenue authorities\non account of arrears of revenue or on\naccount of demanda recoverable as such\narrears,\n\nshall not be brought after the expiration of one year\nfrom the date on which the sale! is confirmed or would\notherwise have become final or conclusive had no such\naction been brought or when the attachment ceased or\ntransfer or payment was made; as the case may be.\n\nACTIONS TO RECOVER LAND AND RENT."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"9. (1) No action shall be brought by any person to\nrecover any land after the expiration of twelve years\nfrom the date on which the right of action accrued to\nhim, or if it first accrued to some person through whom\nhe claims, to that person.\n\n(2) Nothing in this section or in sub-section (2) of\nsection 11 of this Ordinance shall be deemed to affect\nthe provisions of the Crown Suits Ordinance, the\nMalacca Resurveys Ordinance or the Malacca Lands\nCustomary Rights Ordinance of the Straits Settle-\nments or the Penang Corrected Resurveys Ordinance,\n1950, or to apply—\n\n(a) to the Ruler of any State, in respect of State\nland or land reserved for a public purpose\nsituate in such State; or\n\n(b) to any person registered under or by virtue\nof the provisions of the Land! Code of the\nFederated Malay States or of any corres-\nponding Land Enactment in force in any\nState as the proprietor of the land sought\nto be recovered, or to any person claiming\nthrough a person so registered, except to\nthe extent that such Code or Enactment so\nprovides or permits."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"10. (1) Where the person bringing an action to\nrecover land or some person through whom he claims\nhas been in possession thereof and has, whilst entitled\nthereto, been dispossessed or discontinued his\npossession, the right; of action shall be deemed to\nhave accrued on the date of the dispossession or\ndiscontinuance.    ]\n\n(2) Where any person brings an action to recover\nany land of a deceas¢d person whether under a will or\nintestacy and the deceased person was on the date of\n\nhis death in possession of the land and was the last\n|\n\nLIMITATION.                    27\nperson entitled to the land to be ih possession thereof\nthe cause of action shall be deemefl to have accrued on\nthe date of his death.\n\n(3) Where any person brings/an action to recover\nland, being an estate or interest in possession assured\notherwise than by will to him, or to some person\nthrough whom he claims, by a person who, at the date\nwhen the assurance took effedt, was in possession of\nthe land, or in the case of a rgnt charge created by the\nassurance, in possession of the land charged, and no\nperson has been in possession of the land by virtue of\nthe assurance, the right of Action shall be deemed to\nhave accrued on the date /when the assurance took\nelect.\n\n(4) A right of action to/recover land by virtue of a\nforfeiture or breach of condition shall be deemed to\nhave accrued on the date/on which the forfeiture was\nincurred or the condition broken :\n\nProvided that, if su¢h a right has accrued to a\nperson entitled to an estate or interest in reversion or\nremainder and the land was not recovered by virtue\nthereof, the right of action to recover the land shall\nnot be deemed to haye accrued to that person until\nhis estate or interest fell into possession, as if no\nsuch forfeiture or byeach of condition had occurred."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"11. (1) Subject as/hereafter in this section provided,\nthe right of action to recover any land shall, in a case\nwhere the estate oy interest claimed was an estate or\ninterest in reversign or remainder or any other future\nestate or interest nd no person has taken possession\nof the land by virtue of the estate or interest claimed,\nbe deemed to haye accrued on the date on which the\nestate or interest/ fell into possession by-the determina-\ntion of the pregeding estate or interest.\n\n(2) If the person entitled to the preceding estate\nor interest, not/ being a term of years absolute, was not\nin possession gf the land on the date of the determina-\ntion thereof, no action shall be brought by the person\nentitled to the succeeding estate or interest after the\nexpiration of twelve years from the date on which the\nright of action accrued to the person entitled to the\npreceding ¢state or interest, or six years from the\ndate on ee the right of action accrued to the person\n\nentitled to/the succeeding estate or interest, whichever\nperiod last expires.\n\nAccrual of\nright of\naction in\ncase of\nfuture\ninterests\nin land.\n\nProvisions\nin case of\nsettled\nland and\nland held\non trust.\n\n28            No. 4 oF 1953,\n\n(3) No person shall bring an/ action to recover any\nestate or interest in land under an assurance taking\neffect after the right of action fo recover the land had\naccrued to the person by whom the assurance was made\nor some person through whom he claimed or some\nperson entitled to a preceding estate or interest, unless\nthe action is brought within the period during which\nthe person by whom the assurance was made could\nhave brought such an action.\n\n(4) Where any person is entitled to any estate or\ninterest in land in possession and, while so entitled,\nis also entitled to any futurejestate or interest in that\nland, and his right to recover the estate or interest in\npossession is barred under this Ordinance, no action\nshall be brought by that person, or by any person\nclaiming through him, in respect of the future estate\nor interest, unless in the meantime possession of the\nland has been recovered by a person entitled to an\nintermediate estate or interest."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"12. (1) Subject to the provisions of sub-section (1)\nof section 22 of this Ordinance, the provisions of this\nOrdinance shall apply to equitable interests in land,\nincluding interests in the proceeds of the sale of land\nheld upon trust for sale, in like manner as they apply\nto legal estates, and accofdingly a right of action to\nrecover the land shall,/for the purposes of this\nOrdinance but not otherwise, be deemed to accrue to a\nperson entitled in possgssion to such an equitable\ninterest in the like manner and circumstances and on\nthe same date as it would accrue if his interest were\na legal estate in the land.\n\n(2) Where any land is held upon trust including a\ntrust for sale, and the period prescribed by this\nOrdinance (if any) has expired for the bringing of an\naction to recover the land by the trustees, the estate of\nthe trustees shall not be extinguished if and so long\nas the right of action to recover the land of any person\nentitled to a beneficial) interest in the land! or in the\nproceeds of sale either has not accrued or has not been\nbarred by this Ordinance, but if and when every such\nright of action has been so barred, the estate of the\ntrustees shall be a\n\n(3) Where any lan  is held upon trust, including\na trust for sale, an action to recover the land may be\nbrought by the trustees on behalf of any person\nentitled to a benefidial interest in possession in the\n\nLIMITATIDN.                                29\n\nland or in the proceeds of sale whose right of action\nhas not been barred by this Ordinance, notwith-\nstanding that the right of ation of the trustees would\napart from this provision have been barred by this\nOrdinance.\n\n(4) Where any land held on trust for sale is in the\npossession of a person entitled to a beneficial interest\nin the land or in the proceeds of sale, not being a\nperson solely and absolutely entitled thereto, no right\nof action to recover the land shall be deemed for the\npurposes of this Ordinance to accrue during such\npossession to any person/in whom the land is vested\nas trustee, or to any jother person entitled to a\nbeneficial interest in the land or the proceeds of sale."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"13. (1) A tenancy at will shall, for the purposes\nof this Ordinance, be deemed to be determined at the\nexpiration of a period of one year from the commence-\nment thereof, unless it has previously been determined,\nand accordingly the right of action of the person\nentitled to the land subject to the tenancy shall be\ndeemed to have  agcrued  on the date of such\ndetermination.                 |\n\nal\n\n(2) A tenancy from year to year or other period,\nwithout a lease in writing, shall, for the purposes of\nthis Ordinance, be /deemed to be determined at the\nexpiration of the /first year or other period, and\naccordingly the right of action of the person entitled\nto the land subject to the tenancy shall be deemed to\nhave accrued at the date of such determination.\n\n(3) Where any rent has subsequently to the\ndetermination of any tenancy been received in respect\nof the tenancy, the right of action shall be deemed to\nhave accrued on the date of the last receipt of rent.\n\n(4) Where any person is in possession of land by\nvirtue of a lease/in writing by which a rent of not less\nthan ten dollarg is reserved, and the rent is received\nby some person/ wrongfully claiming to be entitled to\nthe land in reversion immediately expectant on the\ndetermination pf the lease, and no rent is subsequently\nreceived by the person rightfully so entitled, the right\nof action of the last-named person to recover the land\nshall be deemed to have accrued at the date when the\nrent was first/received by the person wrongfully claim-\ning as aforesaid and not at the date of the determi-\nnation of the lease.\n\nAccrual of\nright of\naction in\ncase of\ncertain\ntenancies.\n\nKa Ruby m\nL339 /58\n\nAccrual of\nright of\naction in\ncase of\nforfeiture\nor breach\nof condition.\n\nRight of\naction not\nto accrue\nor continue\nunless\nthere is\nadverse\npossession.\n\nLimitation\nof redemp-\n\ntion actions,\n\n—\"—\n\n30           No. 4 or 1/958,\n\n(5) This section shall not apply to any tenancy at\nwill or lease granted by\n\nby the Government of the Federation or of any State\ner-settlonent .\n\n14, A right of action to recover land by virtue of a\nforfeiture or breach of condition shall be deemed to\nhave accrued on the date on! which the forfeiture was\nincurred or the condition broken :\n\nProvided that, if such a right has accrued to a\nperson entitled to an estate or interest in reversion or\nremainder and the land was not recovered by virtue\nthereof, the right of action to recover the land shall\nnot be deemed to have agcrued to that person until\nhis estate or interest fell into possession, as if no such\nforfeiture or breach of wT an had occurred."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"15. (1) No right of action to recover land shall be\ndeemed to accrue unless the land is in the possession\nof some person in whose favour the period of limitation\ncan run (hereafter in /this section referred to as\n‘‘adverse possession') and where under the foregoing\nprovisions of this Ordinance any such right of action\nis deemed to accrue on d certain date and no person is\nin adverse possession on that date, the right of action\nshall not be deemed to accrue unless and until adverse\npossession is taken of the land.\n\n(2) Where a right jof action to recover land has\naccrued and thereafter, before the right is barred,\nthe land ceases to be fin adverse possession, the right\nof action shall no lomger be deemed to have accrued\nand no fresh right of/action shall be deemed to accrue\nunless and until the land is again taken into adverse\npossession.\n\n(3) For the purpdses of this section—\n\n(a) possession of any land subject to a rent charge\nby a pergon (other than the person entitled\nto the rent charge) who does not pay the\nrent shall be deemed to be adverse posses-\nsion of /the rent charge; and\n\n(b) receipt of/ rent under a lease by a person\nwrongfully claiming, in accordance with\nsub-section (4) of section 13 of this\nOrdinance, the land in reversion shall be\ndeemefl to be adverse possession of the land."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"16. When a mortgagee of land has been in posses-\nsion of any of the mortgaged land for a period of\ntwelve years, no action to redeem the land of which\n\nLIMITATION.            31\nthe mortgagee has been so in/possession shall there-\nafter be brought by the mortgagor or any person\n-claiming through him:\n\nProvided that where a mortgagee is by virtue of\nthe mortgage in possession of any mortgaged land and\neither receives any sum in respect of the principal or\ninterest of the mortgage debt or acknowledges in\naccordance with the provisign of section 27 of this\nOrdinance the title of the mortgagor, or his equity of\nredemption, an action to /redeem the land in his\npossession may be brought/ at any time before the\nexpiration of twelve years from the date of the\npayment or acknowledgment."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"17. For the purposes of/this Ordinance, no person\nshall be deemed to have been in possession of any land\nby reason only of having made a formal entry thereon,\nand no continual or other Claim upon or near any land\nshall preserve any right  F action to recover the land."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"18. At the determination of the period limited by\nthis Ordinance to any person for bringing an action to\nrecover land the right and title of such person to the\nland for the recovery whereof such action might have\nbeen brought within such period, shall be extinguished."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"19. For the purpos¢s of the provisions of this\nOrdinance relating to actions for the recovery of land\nan adiministrator of the estate of a deceased person\nshall be deemed to claim as if there had been no\ninterval of time between the death of the deceased\nperson and the grant of the letters of administration."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"20. No action shall/be brought, or distress made, to\nrecover arrears of rent, or damages in respect thereof,\nafter the expiration/ of six years from the date on\nwhich the arrears became due.\n\nACTIONS TO RECOVER: MONEY SECURED BY\nMORTGAGE OR GHARGE OR TO RECOVER PRO-\nCHEDS QF THE SALE OF LAND."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"21. (1) No action shall be brought to recover any\nprincipal sum of money secured by a mortgage or other\ncharge on land or personal property or to enforce such\nmortgage or charge, or to recover proceeds of the sale\nof land or persoyal property after the expiration of\nm the date when the right to receive\nthe money accruéd.\n\nNo right of\naction to be\npreserved\nby formal\nentry or\ncontinual\nclaim,\n\nRight of\nperson out\nof posses-\nsion extin-\nguished.\n\nAdminis-\ntrator's\n\nclaim to\ndate back\nto death.\n\nLimitation\nof actions\nto recover\nrent.\n\nLimitation\nof actions\nto recover\nmoney\nsecured by\nmortgage or\ncharge or to\nrecover\nproceeds of\nthe sale of\nland.\n\na\n\n32            No. 4 or 1953.\n\npersonal property shall be brought after the expiration\nof twelve years from the date on which the right to\nforeclose accrued :\n\nProvided that if, after that date the mortgagee was\nin possession of the mortgaged property, the right to\nforeclose on the property which was in his possession\nshall not, for the purposes of this sub-section, be\ndeemed to have accrued until the date on which his\n\npossession discontinued.\n\n(2) No foreclosure action J respect of mortgaged\n\n(3) The right to receive any principal sum of money\nsecured by a mortgage or other charge and the right\nto foreclose on the property subject to the mortgage or\ncharge shall not be deemed to accrue so long as that\nproperty comprises any future interests or any life\ninsurance policy which fhas not matured or been\ndetermined.\n\n(4) Nothing in the preceding sub-sections of this\nsection shall apply to a foreclosure action in respect\nof mortgaged land but the provisions of this Ordinance\nrelating to actions to recover land shall apply to such\nan action.\n\n(5) No action to recover arrears of interest payable\nin respect of any sum off money secured by a mortgage\nor other charge or payable in respect of proceeds of\nthe sale of land, or to /recover damages in respect of\nsuch arrears shall be brought after the expiration of\nsix years from the date on which the interést became\ndue :\n\nProvided that—                             .\n\n(a) where a prigr mortgagee or other incum-\nbrancer has been in possession of the\nproperty mortgaged or charged, and an\naction is /brought within one year of the\ndiscontinuance of such possession by the\nsubsequent incumbrancer, he may recover\nby that. action all the arrears of interest\nwhich fell due during the period of\n\nion by the prior incumbrancer or\nin respect thereof, notwith-\nthat the period exceeded six\n\n(6) where the property subject to the mortgage or\ncharge /comprises any future interest or\nlife insurance policy and it is a term of the\nmortgage or charge that arrears of interest\n\nLIMITATION).                                  33\n\nshall be treated as/part of the principal\nsum of money secuyed by the mortgage or\ncharge, interest shall not be deemed to\nbecome due before the right to receive the\nprincipal sum of money has accrued or is\ndeemed to have actrued.\n\n(6) This section shall not apply to any mortgage or\ncharge on a ship.\n\nACTIONS IN RESPECT OF TRUST PROPERTY OR THE\nPERSONAL ESTATE OF DECEASED PERSONS."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"22. (1) No period of limitation prescribed by this\nOrdinance shall apply to an action by a beneficiary\nunder a trust, being an action—\n\n(a) in respect of any fraud or fraudulent breach\nof trust to which the trustee was a party\nor privy; or |\n\n(b) to recover from the trustee trust property or\nthe proceeds thereof in the possession of\nthe trustee, dr previously received by the\ntrustee and converted to his use.\n\n(2) Subject as aforesaid, an action by a beneficiary\nto recover trust property or in respect of any breach\nof trust, not being an/action for which a period of\nlimitation is prescribed by any other provision of this\nOrdinance, shall not be brought after the expiration\nof six years from the date on which the right of action\naccrued :\n\nProvided that the right of action shall not be deemed\nto have accrued to any beneficiary entitled to a future\ninterest in the trust /property, until the interest fell\ninto possession.\n\n(3) No beneficiary/as against whom there would be\na good defence under this Ordinance shall derive any\ngreater or other benefit from a judgment or order\nobtained by any other beneficiary than he could have\nobtained if he had brought the action and this\nOrdinance had peep pleaded in defence."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II."},"text":{"en":"23. Subject to the provisions of sub-section (1) of\nsection 22 of this/Ordinance, no action in respect of\nany claim to the personal estate of a deceased person\nor to any share jor interest in such estate, whether\nunder a will or on intestacy, shall be brought after the\nexpiration of twelve years from the date when the\n\nLimitation.\nof actions\nin respect\nof trust\nproperty.\n\nLimitation\nof actions\nclaiming\npersonal\nestate of a\ndeceased\nperson.\n\nExtension\nof limita-\ntion period\nin onse of\ndisnbility.\n\n34            No. 4 or 1953,\n\nright to receive the share or interest accrued, and no\naction to recover arrears of inter¢st in respect of any\nlegacy, or damages in respect of such arrears, shall be\nbrought after the expiration of six years from the\ndate on which the interest became due.\n\nPart III.\n\n24, (1) If on the date when any right of action\naccrued for which a period of /limitation is prescribed\nby this Ordinance, the person/to whom it accrued was\nunder a disability, the action may be brought at any\ntime before the expiration off six years, or in the case\nof actions to which sub-section (4) of section 6 or\nsection 8 of this Ordinance applies, one year from the\ndate when such person ceas¢d to be under a disability\nor died, whichever event first occurred, notwithstand-\ning that the period of limitation had expired :\n\nProvided that in any case to which the provisions\nof section 29 of this Ordinance apply, this sub-section\nshall apply as if the date from which the period of\n|                were substituted for the\ndate when the right of dction accrued.\n\n(2) Where any such person as is referred to in sub-\nsection (1) of this section was on such date under two\ndisabilities or where before the disability which he\nwas under on such date had ceased he was affected by\nanother disability he shall be deemed for the purposes\nof this section to have continued under a disability\nuntil both such disabilities have ceased.\n\nis under any such /disability, and when a discharge\ncan be given without the concurrence of such person,\ntime will run against them all. Where no such\ndischarge can be given, time will not run as against\nany of them until all such persons cease to be under\na disability or uptil one of them becomes capable of\n\n(3) When one of os joint-creditors or claimants\n\nwhere the right of action first accrued to\nsome person not under a disability through\nwhom the person under a disability claims;\n\nLIMITATION.                                35\n\n(6) when a right of action which has accrued to a\n\n(c) no\n\nperson under a disability accrues, on the\ndeath of that person while still under a\ndisability, to another person under a\ndisability, no further extension of time\nshall be allowed by reason of the disability\nof the second person;\n\naction to recover land or money charged on\nland for which a/period of limitation is\nprescribed under this Ordinance shall be\nbrought by virtue/of the provisions of this\nsection by any person after the expiration\nof thirty years fyom the date on which the\nright of action accrued to that person or\nsome person through whom he claims;\n\n(d) nothing in such provisions shall apply to any\n\naction to reco a penalty or forfeiture,\nor sum by way thereof, by virtue of any\nwritten law, except where the action is\nbrought by an/ aggrieved party."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III."},"text":{"en":"25. Where letters of administration to the estate of\na creditor have been granted to his debtor, the running\nof the time prescribed /for an action to recover the\ndebt shall be suspended while the administration\ncontinues."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III."},"text":{"en":"26. (1) Where there/has accrued any right of action\n\nto recover land or to ¢nforce a mortgage or charge in\nrespect of land or personal property, and—\n\n(a) the person fin possession of the land or\n\npersonal property acknowledges the title of\nthe person to whom the right of action has\naccrued ;/or\n\n(b) in the case jof any such action by a mortgagee\n\nor changee the person in possession as\naforesajd or the person liable for the debt\nby the mortgage or charge makes\nent in respect thereof, whether of\nprincipal or interest,\n\nthe right shall b¢ deemed to have accrued on and not\nbefore the date of the acknowledgment or last payment.\n\n(2) Where any right of action has accrued to recover\n\nany debt or other liquidated pecuniary claim, or any\n\nExtension\nof limita-\ntion period\nwhere\ndebtor\nadministers\nestate of his\ncreditor.\n\nFresh\naccrual of\naction on\nacknow-\nledgment\nor part\npayment.\n\nFormal\nprovisions\nas to\nacknow-\nledgments\nand part\npayments.\n\nEffect of\nacknow-\nledgment\n\nor part\npayment\n\nou persons\nother than\nthe maker\nor recipient.\n\n36            No. 4 or 1958,\n\nclaim to the personal estate of a deceased person or to\nany share or interest therein, And the person liable or\naccountable therefor acknowledges the claim or makes\nany payment in respect thereof, the right shall be\ndeemed to have accrued on and! not before the date of\nthe acknowledgment or the last payment :\n\ninterest due at any time shall not extend the period\nfor claiming the remainder/of the rent or interest then\ndue, but any payment of ipterest shall have effect, for\nthe purposes of this sub-section only, as if it were a\npayment in respect of the principal debt.\n\nProvided that a \"ine al of a part of the rent or"}},{"id":"MY-H223-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III."},"text":{"en":"27. (1) Every such acknowledgment as is referred\nto in section 26 or in the proviso to section 16 of this\nOrdinance shall be in writing and signed by the person\nmaking the acknowledgment.\n\n(2) Any such acknowledgment or payment as is\nreferred to in section 26 or the proviso to section 16\nof this Ordinance may be made by the agent of the\nperson by whom it is required to be made under that\nsection, and shall be made to the person, or to an agent\nof the person, whose title or claim is being acknow-\nledged or, as the case may be, in respect of whose\nclaim the payment is being made."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III."},"text":{"en":"28. (1) For the purposes of this Ordinance an\nacknowledgment of the title to any land, or mortgaged\nor charged property by any person in possession\nthereof shall bind all other persons in possession\nduring the ensuing period of limitation.\n\n(2) A payment in respect of a debt secured by a\nmortgage or charge by the mortgagor or any person in\npossession of the mortgaged or charged land or\npersonal property shall, so far as any right of the\nmortgagee or chargee to foreclose or otherwise to\nrecover the pfoperty is concerned, bind all other\npersons in possession of the mortgaged property during\nthe ensuing period of limitation.\n\n(3) Where/there are two or more mortgagors of\nland or personal property and the title or right to\nredemption gf one of the mortgagors is acknowledged\nas aforesaid, the acknowledgment shall be deemed to\nhave been made to all the mortgagors.\n\nLIMITATION).                                  37\n\n(4) An acknowledgment off any debt or other\nliquidated pecuniary claim shall bind the acknow-\nledgor and his successors but not any other person :\n\nProvided that an acknowlédgment made after the\nexpiration of the period of limitation prescribed for\nthe bringing of an action to/recover the debt or other\nclaim shall not bind any/successor on whom the\nliability devolves on the determination of a preceding\nestate or interest in property under a settlement\ntaking effect before the date of the acknowledgment.\n\n(5) A payment made in respect of any debt or other\nliquidated pecuniary claim shall bind all persons\nliable in respect thereof\n\nProvided that a payment made after the expiration\nof the period of limitation prescribed for the bringing\nof an action to recover/the debt or other claim shall\nnot bind any person other than the person making\nthe payment and his successors, and shall not bind\nany successor on whom the liability devolves on the\ndetermination of a preceding estate or interest in\nproperty under a settlement taking effect before the\ndate of the payment\n\n(6) An acknowledgment by one of several personal\nrepresentatives of amy claim to the personal estate of\na deceased person, gr to any share or interest therein,\nor a payment by one of several personal representatives\nin respect of any such claim shall bind the estate of\nthe deceased an .\n\n(7) In this section the expression ‘\"‘successor,'' in\nrelation to any mortgagee or person liable in respect\nof any debt or claim, means his personal representa-\ntives and any other person on whom the rights under\nthe mortgage or), as the case may be, the liability in\nrespect of the debt or claim devolve, whether on death\nor bankruptcy jor the disposition of property or the\ndetermination of a limited estate or interest in settled\nproperty or otherwise."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III."},"text":{"en":"29. Where, in the case of any action for which a\nperiod of limitation is prescribed by this Ordinance,\neither—\n\n(a) the /action is based upon the fraud of the\nefendant or his agent or of any person\nhrough whom he claims or his agent; or\n(b) the/ right of action is concealed by the fraud\n\ncof any such person as aforesaid; or\n\nPostpone-\nment of\nlimitation\nperiod in\ncase of\nfraud or\nmistake.\n\nApplication\nof Ordinance\nand other\nlimitation\n\"enactments\nto arbitra-\ntions.\n\n38            No. 4 or 1953)\n\n(c) the action is for relief from the consequences\nof a mistake,\n\nthe period of limitation shall not begin to run until\nthe plaintiff has discovered! the/ fraud or the mistake,\nas the case may be, or could with reasonable diligence\nhave discovered it:\n\nProvided that nothing in this section shall enable\nany action to be brought to rover, or enforce any\ncharge against, or set aside any transaction affecting,\nany property which—\n\n(i) in the case of fraud, has been purchased for\nvaluable consideration by a person who was\nnot a party to the fraud and did not at the\ntime of the pufchase know or have reason\nto believe that any fraud had been\ncommitted; or\n\n(ii) in the case of mistake, has been purchased for\nvaluable corsideration, subsequently to\nthe transaction in which the mistake was\nmade, by a/person who did not know or\nhave reason to believe that the mistake\nhad been made.\n\nPart IV."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30"},"chapter":{"en":"Part IV."},"text":{"en":"30. (1) This Ordinance and any other written law\nrelating to the limitation of actions shall apply to\narbitrations as they apply to actions.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding any term in any submission to\nthe effect that no cfs of action shall accrue in respect\nof any matter required by the submission to be referred\nuntil an award js made under the submission, the\ncause of action shall, for the purpose of this Ordinance\nand of any other such written law (whether in their\napplication to arbitrations or to other proceedings),\nbe deemed to have accrued in respect of any such\nmatter at the time when it would have accrued but for\nthat term in ie submission.\n\n(3) For the purpose of this Ordinance and of any\nsuch written haw as aforesaid, an arbitration shall be\ndeemed to be commenced when one party to the\narbitration serves on the other party or parties a\nuotice requiring him or them to appoint an arbitrator\nor to agreg to the appointment of an arbitrator, or,\nwhere the submission provides that the reference shall\n\nwt\n\nLIMITATION,                                       39\n\nbe to a person named or designated in the submission,\nrequiring him or them to submit the/ dispute to the\nperson so named or designated.\n\n(4) Any such notice as aforesai\neither—\n(a) by delivering it to the person on whom it is\nto be served; or\n\n(b) by leaving it at the uspal or last known\nplace of abode in the/ Federation of that\n\nperson; or\n\n(c) by sending it by post yn a registered letter\naddressed to that person at his usual\n\nor last known place of abode in the\nFederation,\n\nas well as in any other. mannér provided in the sub-\nmission ; and where a notice is/sent by post in a manner\nprescribed by paragraph (c) of this sub-section, service\nthereof shall, unless the contrary is proved, be deemed\nto have been effected at thg time at which the letter\nwould have been delivered/in the ordinary course of\npost.\n\n(5) Where the High Cotrt orders that an award be\nset aside or orders, after the commencement of an\narbitration, that the arbitration shall cease to have\neffect with respect to the dispute referred, the Court\nmay further order that the period between the\ncommencement of the arbitration and the date of the\norder of the Court shall be excluded in computing\nthe time prescribed by this Ordinance or any such\nwritten law as aforesaid for the commencement of\nproceedings (including arbitration) with respect to the\ndispute referred.\n\n(6) This section ghall apply to an arbitration under\nany written law ag well as to an arbitration pursuant\nto a submission, dnd sub-sections (3) and (4) thereof\nshall have effect, /in relation to an arbitration under\nany written law, as if for the references to the\nsubmission inet were substituted references to such\nof the provisions of the law or of any order, scheme,\nrules, regulatigns, or bye-laws made thereunder as\nrelate to the arbitration.\n\n(7) In this/section the expressions \"‘arbitration'',\n‘\"‘award'' and ‘‘submission'' have the same meanings\nas in the Aybitration Ordinance, 1950.\n\nmay be served\n\nNo. 12 of\n\nProvisions\n\nas to set-off\n\nor counter-\nclaim,\n\nAcquies-\ncence.\n\nApplication\nto the\n\nthe Govern-\n\nment.\n\nDa\n\ndenak\n\ndn 33303\n\ndin. snfog State\n\nProvisions\nas to\nactions\nalready\nbarred and\npending\nactions.\n\n40            No. 4 or 19538"}},{"id":"MY-H223-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31"},"chapter":{"en":"Part IV."},"text":{"en":"31. For the purposes of this Ordinance, any claim\nby way of set-off or counterclaim shall be deemed to\nbe a separate action and to haye been commenced on\nthe same date as the action im which the set-off or\ncounterclaim is pleaded."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A32","no":32,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 32"},"chapter":{"en":"Part IV."},"text":{"en":"32. Nothing in this Ordimance shall affect any\nequitable jurisdiction to refuse relief on the ground\nof acquiescence, laches or otherwise."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A33","no":33,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 33"},"chapter":{"en":"Part IV."},"text":{"en":"33. (1) Save as in this Ordinance otherwise pro-\nvided and without prejudice to the provisions of\nsection 3 of this Ordinance{ this Ordinance shall apply\nto proceedings by or against the-Crewn-er the Govern-\nment in like manner ag it applies to proceedings\nbetween subjects and /for the purposes of this\nOrdinance a proceeding; by petition of right shall be\ndeemed to be commenced on the date on which the\npetition is presented :\n\nProvided that this Ordinance shall not apply to any\nproceedings                by the Government for\nthe recovery of any tax, duty or interest thereon or to\nany forfeiture proceedings under any written law in\nforce in the Federation relating to customs duties or\nexcise or to any proceedings in respect of the forfei-\nture of a ship.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this section proceedings by\nor against any Government Department or any officer\nof any Government as such or any\n\nperson acting on behalf ef+he—CGrewn—er of the\nGovernment shall be deemed to be proceedings by or\nagainst           the Government as—the—ease\n\nmybe\n(3) In this section the expression \"the Government''\n\nshall be oie ed to include the Government of any\n\n34, Nothing in this Ordinance shall—\n\n(a) enable any action to be brought which was\nbarred before the commencement of this\nOrdinance by any Ordinance or Enactment\nrepealed by this Ordinance, except in so\nfar as the cause of action or right of action\nmay be revived by an acknowledgment or\npart payment made in accordance with the\nprovisions of this Ordinance; or\n\n|\n\nLIMITATION.                                  41\n\n(d) affect any action or Jarbitration commenced\n\nbefore the commen\n\nement of this Ordinance\n\nor the title to any property which is the\nsubject of any sugh action or arbitration."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A35","no":35,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 35"},"chapter":{"en":"Part IV."},"text":{"en":"35. The Ordinance and the Enactments specified in\n\nthe Schedule to this Ordina\n\ne are hereby repealed."}},{"id":"MY-H223-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36"},"chapter":{"en":"Part IV."},"text":{"en":"36. The Limitation (Eneniy Occupation) Ordinance,\n\n1946, shall have effect as i\n\nthe reference therein to\n\n\"existing laws'' had included a reference to this\nOrdinance.\nTHE SCHEDULE.\n(Secfion 35.)\n8.8. Cap. 16           ..       The Limitation Ordinance\nF.M.S. Cap. 18 ...               The Limitation Enactment\n\nJohore Enactment No. 23\nKelantan Enactment No. 4 of 193\nKedah Enactment No. 60         st\nTrengganu Enactment No. 20 of/1356\nPerlis Enactment No. 3 of 134\n\nThe Limitation Enactment\n\nThe Limitation Enactment, 1930\nEnactment No. 60 (Limitation)\nLimitation Enactment, 1356\nLimitation Enactment, 1344\n\nRepeal.\n\nThe Limita-\ntion (Enemy\nOccupation)\nOrdinance,\n1946, to\napply to\nthis Ordi-\nnance.\nNo. 4 of"}}],"pack":"my-5"};
  FT["MY-H2230"] = {"id":"MY-H2230","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 196/1982&status=PINDAAN","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"1982年法律修订（《1953年氰化氢（熏蒸）法》）令","en":"REVISION OF LAWS (HYDROGEN CYANIDE (FUMIGATION) ACT 1953) ORDER 1982","orig":"REVISION OF LAWS (HYDROGEN CYANIDE (FUMIGATION) ACT 1953) ORDER 1982","ms":"Perintah Semakan Undang-Undang (Akta Hidrogen Sianida (Pengasapan) 1953) 1982","vi":"Lệnh về Sửa đổi pháp luật (Luật Axit Xianhiđric (Khử trùng) 1953) năm 1982","th":"คำสั่งการปรับปรุงกฎหมาย (พระราชบัญญัติไฮโดรเจนไซยาไนด์ (การรมยา) ค.ศ. 1953) ค.ศ. 1982","id":"Perintah Revisi Peraturan Perundang-undangan (Undang-Undang Asam Sianida (Fumigasi) 1953) Tahun 1982"},"level":"regulation","category":"01_宪法与基础法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA196","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"1982","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\01_宪法与基础法\\1982_P.U.(A)196-1982_REVISION OF LAWS (HYDROGEN CYANIDE (FUMIGATION) ACT 1953) ORDER 1982.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H2230-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Keselamatan Dalam\n\nNegeri (Kawasan Sekatan) 1982 dan hendaklah mula berkuatkuasa ku\n\npada 1hb Julai 1982."}},{"id":"MY-H2230-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Kawasan yang diperihalkan dalam Jadual di bawah ini adalah\ndiisytiharkan sebagai kawasan sekatan.\n\nJADUAL\n\nSeluruh kawasan yang diisytiharkan sebagai kawasan\nkawalan dalam Jadual Pertama Perintah Keselamatan Dalam\nNegeri (Kawasan Kawalan) yang disiarkan sebagai LN. 214\npada 25hb Ogos 1960, seperti yang dipinda dari semasa ke\nsemasa, tidak termasuk kawasan-kawasan yang diisytiharkan\nsebagai Kawasan Kediaman dalam Jadual Kedua Perintah itu\ndan jalan-jalan raya yang tersebut dalam Jadual Keempat\nPerintah itu.\n\nDiperbuat pada 24hb Jun 1982.\n[KHEDN. Y. 14/TII/D; PN. (PU?) 216.\n\nDato' Musa HitaM,\nMenteri Hal Ehwal Dalam Negeri\n\nP.U. (A)\n78/73.\n\nNama dan\nmula berkuat-\nasa.\n\nPerisytiharan\nkawasan\nsekatan.\n\nP.U. (A) 195-196.                     658\n\nP.U. (A)\n\nCitation and\ncommence-\nment.\n\nDeclaration\nof restricted\narea.\n\nAkta 1\n\nNama dan\nmula ber-\nkuatkuasa.\n\nPembetulan\nAkta 260.\n\nINTERNAL SECURITY ACT 1960\nINTERNAL SECURITY (RESTRICTED ARBA) ORDER 1982\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by regulation 3 of the Internal\nSecurity (Restricted Articles) Regulations 1973, the Minister makes\nthe following Order:\n\n1. This Order may be cited as the Internal Security (Restricted\nArea) Order 1982 and shall come into force on the Ist July 1982.\n\n2. The area described in the Schedule hereto is declared to be a\nrestricted area.\nSCHEDULE\n\nThe whole area declared as the controlled area in the First\nSchedule of the Internal Seourity (Controlled Area) Order\npublished as LN. 214 on 25th August 1960, as may from time\nto time be amended, excluding the areas declared as the\nResidential Areas in the Second Schedule thereof and the\nroads specified in the Fourth Schedule thereof.\n\nMade the 24th June 1982,\n[KHEDN. Y. 14/TII/D; PN. (PU?) 216.)\n\nDato' Musa Hiram,\nMinister of Home Affairs\n\nP.U. (A) 196.\nAKTA PENYEMAKAN UNDANG-UNDANG 1968\n\nPERINTAH PENYEMAKAN Undang-Undang (Akta HIDROGEN\nSIANID) (PEWASAPAN) 1953) 1982\n\nPada menjalankan kuasa-kuasa yang diberi oleh seksyen 15 Akta\nPenyemakan Undang-Undang 1968, Pesuruhjaya Penyemak\nUndang-Undang, dengan kelulusan Jawatankuasa Penyemakan\nUndang-Undang, membuat Perintah yang berikut:\n\n1, Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Penyemakan\nUndang-Undang (Akta Hidrogen Sianid (Pewasapan) 1953) 1982\ndan hendaklah disifatkan telah mula berkuatkuasa pada 24hb\nDisember 1981.\n\n2. Akta Hidrogen Sianid (Pewasapan) 1953 adalah diperbetulkan\ndengan menggantikan perkataan \"internment\" yang terdapat di\nbaris akhir seksyen 6 (2) Akta dengan perkataan \"interment\".\n\nDiperbuat pada 17hb Jun 1982.\n(PN. (S.U. 2) 159; PN. (PU?) 231.)\n\nTan Sri DATUK CHANG Min Tat,\nPesuruhjaya Penyemak Undang-Undang,\nMalaysia\n\n659                       P.U. (A) 196-197.\n\nSS EDARAN AAA a\nf\n\nREVISION OF LAWS ACT 1968\n\nREVISION OF LAws (HYDROGEN CYANIDE (FUMIGATION)\nAct 1953) Order 1982\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 15 of the Revision Ac: 1.\nof Laws Act 1968, the Commissioner of Law Revision, with the\napproval of the Law Revision Committee, makes the following\nOrder:\n\n1. This Order may be cited as the Revision of Laws (Hydrogen Citation and\nCyanide (Fumigation) Act 1953) Order 1982 and shall be deemed trent\"\nto have come into force on 24th December 1981.\n\n2. The Hydrogen Cyanide (Fumigation) Act 1953 is rectified Rectification\nby substituting the word \"interment\" for the word \"internment\" * \"7\nappearing in the last line of section 6 (2) of the Act.\n\nMade the 17th June 1982.\n(PN. (S.U. 2) 159; PN. (PU?) 231.)\n\nTAN Sri DATUK CHANG MIN Tar,\nCommissioner of Law Revision,\nMalaysia\n\nP.U. (A) 197.\nORDINAN PERUSAHAAN NENAS 1957\n\nPERATURAN-PERATURAN PERUSAHAAN NENAS (BANTUAN KEWANGAN\nUNTUK TANAM SEMULA) (PINDAAN) 1982\n\nPada menjalankan kuasa-kuasa yang di beri oleh seksyen 25\nOrdinan Perusahaan Nenas 1957, Lembaga dengan kelulusan 13/57,\nMenteri membuat peraturan-peraturan berikut :\n\n1. Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan- Nama dan\nperaturan Perusahaan Nenas (Bantuan Kewangan Untuk Tanam iitiwsca.\nSemula) (Pindaan) 1982 dan hendaklah disifatkan telah mula\nberkuatkuasa pada 1hb Januari 1974.\n\n2, Peraturan 8 Peraturan-peraturan Perusahaan Nenas (Bantuan Pindaan\nKewangan Untuk Tanam Semula) 1971 (selepas daripada ini Dy\"¢%\\\"™\ndisebut Peraturan-peraturan ibu) adalah dipinda—                   406/71.\n\n(a) dengan menggantikan ruangan (1) dan (2) perenggan (1)\ndengan yang berikut:\n(1)                  (2)\n\"(a) Bowers with 15 acres or the whole\ness\n\n(b) growers with more than 15 2/3 of the holding\nacres but less than 100 subject to a minimum\nACTOS                    of 15 acres\"; dan\n\n(b) dengan menggantikan perkataan-perkataan \"items (b) and\n(c)\" dalam perenggan (2) dengan perkataan \"item (b)\"."}}],"pack":"my-5"};
  FT["MY-H2231"] = {"id":"MY-H2231","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 196/2011&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2011年银行与金融机构（持牌外国电子货币经纪）（豁免）令","en":"BANKING AND FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS (LICENSED FOREIGN ELECTRONIC MONEY-BROKER) (EXEMPTION) ORDER 2011","orig":"BANKING AND FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS (LICENSED FOREIGN ELECTRONIC MONEY-BROKER) (EXEMPTION) ORDER 2011","ms":"Perintah Perbankan dan Institusi Kewangan (Broker Wang Elektronik Asing Berlesen) (Pengecualian) 2011","vi":"Lệnh về Ngân hàng và tổ chức tài chính (Nhà môi giới tiền điện tử nước ngoài được cấp phép) (Miễn trừ) năm 2011","th":"คำสั่งการธนาคารและสถาบันการเงิน (นายหน้าตราอิเล็กทรอนิกส์ต่างชาติที่ได้รับใบอนุญาต) (การยกเว้น) ค.ศ. 2011","id":"Perintah Perbankan dan Lembaga Keuangan (Pialang Uang Elektronik Asing Berizin) (Pembebasan) Tahun 2011"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA196","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2011","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 3 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2011_P.U.(A)196-2011_BANKING AND FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS (LICENSED FOREIGN ELECTRONIC MONEY-BROKER) (EXEMPTION) ORDER.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H2231-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Bank dan Institusi -Institusi\nKewangan (Broker Wang Asing Elektronik Berlesen) (Pengecualian) 2011 .\nTafsiran"}},{"id":"MY-H2231-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Dalam Perintah ini―\n\"broker wang asing elektronik berlesen\" ertinya suatu broker wang berlesen yang\nmana pengawalnya adalah suatu institusi asing dan menjalankan perniagaan\npembrokeran wang elektronik; dan\n\"perniagaan pembrokeran wang elektronik\" ertinya perniagaan pembrokeran\nwang yang dijalankan melalui suatu sistem pemadanan harga elektronik.\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H2231-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Suatu broker wang asing elektronik berlesen dikecualikan daripada kehendak\nseksyen 36, 38, 39, 40, 41, 42, 45, 46, 51, 52, 55, 57, 58, 60 dan 67 Akta.\nDibuat  10 Jun 2011\n[BNM/JUN 1151/09/13; PN(PU2)479/XV]\nDATO' SERI HAJI AHMAD HUSNI BIN MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\nMenteri Kewangan Kedua\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut subseksyen 118(4) Akta Bank dan\nInstitusi-Institusi Kewangan 1989]\n\nBANKING AND FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS ACT 1989\nBANKING AND FINANCIAL INSTITUTIONS (LICENSED FOREIGN ELECTRONIC\nMONEY-BROKER) (EXEMPTION) ORDER 2011\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 118 (1) of the Banking and Financial\nInstitutions Act 1989 [Act 372], the Minister, on the recommendation of the Bank, makes\nthe following order:\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-5"};
